==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{bor|en|de|Mitose}}, from {{der|en|grc|μίτος||thread}} + {{af|en|-osis}}, probably in reference to the thread-like [[chromatin]] seen during mitosis.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/maɪˈtəʊ.sɪs/}}
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|en|/maɪˈtoʊ.sɪs/}}
* {{rhymes|en|əʊsɪs|s=3}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~|mitoses}}

# {{lb|en|cytology}} The [[division]] of a cell [[nucleus]] in which the [[genome]] is copied and separated into two identical halves. It is normally followed by [[cell division]].

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|karyokinesis}}
* [[karyomitosis]]

====Meronyms====
* {{l|en|prophase}}
* {{l|en|metaphase}}
* {{l|en|anaphase}}
* {{l|en|telophase}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|mitotic}}
* {{l|en|mitotically}}
* {{l|en|transmitosis}}

